<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Research services"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/research-services/"}>{"Research services"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-33"}>{"Evidence synthesis "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-34"}>{"Design & protocol "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-35"}>{"Data & statistics "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Scope the study "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-33"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l sbdrop__l--2"} style={{ '--rows': "4" }}> <a href={"/services/research-services/systematic-review/"}>{"Systematic review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/scoping-review/"}>{"Scoping review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/rapid-review/"}>{"Rapid & targeted review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/living-systematic-review/"}>{"Living systematic review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/evidence-gap-map/"}>{"Evidence gap map"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/meta-analysis/"}>{"Meta-analysis"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/network-meta-analysis/"}>{"Network meta-analysis & ITC"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/umbrella-review/"}>{"Umbrella review"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/literature-review-and-gap/"}>{"Literature review & gap"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-34"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/research-services/experimental-design/"}>{"Experimental design"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/statistical-analysis-plan/"}>{"Statistical analysis plan"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/grant-writing/"}>{"Grant writing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-35"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/research-services/biostatistics-and-statistical-programming-services/"}>{"Biostatistics & programming"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/redcap-database-build/"}>{"REDCap database build"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/data-management-plan/"}>{"Data management plan"}</a> <a href={"/services/research-services/cdisc-sdtm-adam/"}>{"CDISC SDTM & ADaM"}</a> </div> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/research-services/"}>{"Research services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Literature Review and Gap Analysis Service"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Literature Review and Gap Analyses"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"Literature reviews and research gap analysis by Pubrica’s subject matter experts. "}<b>{"Somebody who works in your field reads the literature"}</b>{", appraises it, and says plainly what is missing from it."}</p> <ul className={"hpts"}> <li><b>{"A reproducible search strategy"}</b>{", reported in full so a reviewer can re-run it"}</li> <li><b>{"Critical appraisal and a review matrix"}</b>{" — every study placed against the others on design, population and outcome"}</li> <li><b>{"Gap analysis and evidence mapping"}</b>{", with the gaps ranked by whether they are worth a study"}</li> <li><b>{"Narrative, scoping or integrative"}</b>{", chosen for the question rather than the budget"}</li> <li><b>{"Writing, rewriting and editing"}</b>{" to the guideline your target journal names"}</li> </ul> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Send your topic"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-lr"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-lr"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"Review at a glance"}</b>{" · one completed project"}</span> <span>{"Scoping review · gap map"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Search strategy written and handed over"}</b><span>{"6 databases"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Studies appraised against a named instrument"}</b><span>{"AMSTAR 2, NOS"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Evidence mapped by population and outcome"}</b><span>{"25 cells"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Gaps named, with the study that would fill each"}</b><span>{"5 stated"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Written to the journal or funder's format"}</b><span>{"PRISMA, EQUATOR"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Question"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" search "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" appraisal "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" synthesis "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" gap map "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"proposal"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every review"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Reproducible search"}</li> <li>{"Appraised, not just cited"}</li> <li>{"Gaps named specifically"}</li> <li>{"Evidence tables supplied"}</li> <li>{"Written to your format"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Supporting researchers through publication"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"900,000+"}</b><span>{"Researchers worked with worldwide"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"5,000+"}</b><span>{"Journals and societies"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <nav className={"pagenav is-scroll"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-literature-review-what-we-do-hyweka"} aria-current={"true"}>{"What we do"}</a><a href={"#pn-literature-review-who-we-serve-lifxp4"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-literature-review-our-compliance-kqep5h"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-literature-review-how-it-works-1xe12xi"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-literature-review-our-experts-f0g9ov"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-literature-review-sample-work-3jekwr"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-literature-review-packages-1oyqjie"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-literature-review-guarantee-a6py6n"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-literature-review-client-stories-1ew26zu"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-literature-review-faq-qw26fx"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-what-we-do-hyweka"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we do"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Four areas of work, and each can be commissioned on its own."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Our scientific literature review service is offered in parts, because researchers arrive at every stage — some with a topic, some with two hundred PDFs and no structure."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Search strategy and literature sourcing"}</b> <span>{"A reproducible strategy built from MeSH and Emtree terms with Boolean and proximity operators, adapted for each platform rather than pasted between them, and run across PubMed, MEDLINE, Embase, the Cochrane Library, Scopus, Web of Science, CINAHL and the subject databases your question needs. Grey literature, clinical guidelines, trial registries and regulatory documents where they bear on it. Full texts sourced, deduplicated and delivered as a managed EndNote, Mendeley or Zotero library."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Critical appraisal and the review matrix"}</b> <span>{"Studies screened against pre-set criteria and then appraised, each with the instrument its design calls for — AMSTAR 2, GRADE, ROBIS 1.2, the Newcastle-Ottawa Scale or the JBI instruments — with the judgement recorded per study rather than asserted in aggregate. Data extracted into a structured review matrix and evidence tables: design, setting, population, exposure, comparator, outcomes, effect estimates, funding and limitations, in a file you keep and can extend."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Gap analysis and evidence mapping"}</b> <span>{"The evidence mapped across populations and outcomes, then read for the four kinds of gap: nothing at all, only weak designs, findings that contradict each other, and the population everyone excluded. Each one written as a specific answerable question in PICO or PECO terms, with the study design that would close it — which is the difference between a review that ends and a proposal that starts."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Writing, rewriting and editing"}</b> <span>{"The review written to the structure its destination requires, or an existing draft rewritten — restructured around themes rather than around the order you read things in, with the summarising cut back and the critical evaluation put in, outdated sources replaced, references corrected, and every claim linked back to the research objectives. Language editing, plagiarism and AI-content screening before it goes anywhere."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Types of literature review"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Fifteen types, and which job each one does."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"They are not interchangeable and they are not ranked. The right one is decided by what the review has to survive — an examiner, a funding panel, a notified body or a journal editor."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Systematic literature review"}</b><span>{"A predefined protocol, an exhaustive search and a reproducible method, so that transparency and freedom from selection bias can be demonstrated rather than claimed. Reported under PRISMA."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b><a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/research-services/scoping-review/"}>{"Scoping review"}</a></b><span>{"Maps what evidence exists on a topic and what types it is, identifying key concepts and gaps without appraising study quality. Reported under PRISMA-ScR, and usually the right first move on an unmapped field."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Narrative literature review"}</b><span>{"A descriptive, interpretive account of a broad topic, flexible in scope and the best form for historical development, theoretical context or a live scholarly debate. Honest about being selective."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b><a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/medical-writing/regulatory-writing/state-of-the-art-review/"}>{"State of the art review"}</a></b><span>{"A critical view of the most recent developments in a field — current trends, emerging technologies and where the frontier stops. Ages quickly by design, which is the point."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b><a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/research-services/rapid-review/"}>{"Targeted literature review"}</a></b><span>{"A narrowly defined question or population, answered quickly. Used in clinical and policy settings, and in market access, where a decision has a date on it and a full systematic review does not fit inside it."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b><a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/research-services/rapid-review/"}>{"Rapid review"}</a></b><span>{"Systematic methods with declared shortcuts, for urgent healthcare policy or practice decisions. Balances quality against a deadline by stating what was sacrificed rather than concealing it."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b><a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/research-services/umbrella-review/"}>{"Umbrella review"}</a></b><span>{"A synthesis of existing systematic reviews rather than of studies, giving an overview of a whole field, appraised with AMSTAR 2 and with the overlap between reviews measured rather than assumed."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Cochrane review"}</b><span>{"A systematic review built to Cochrane's own conduct standards and editorial process, which are stricter than the field baseline in screening, extraction and the handling of unpublished data."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Meta-analysis"}</b><span>{"Statistical synthesis of comparable studies into a pooled estimate, with heterogeneity quantified and sensitivity analyses run. Sits inside a systematic review rather than replacing one."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Integrative review"}</b><span>{"Empirical and theoretical literature synthesised together for a holistic view, surfacing patterns, contradictions and emerging themes across methodologically diverse work."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Conceptual review"}</b><span>{"Examines the theories, models and frameworks a field is built on, in order to sharpen a concept or argue for a new theoretical direction. The type most often asked for in a thesis and least often recognised."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Research and methodological review"}</b><span>{"A research review examines empirical studies for their designs, outcomes and quality, identifying methodological strengths and limitations — the source of the gaps a purely topical review never finds."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Expert and scholarly review"}</b><span>{"An expert review assesses the literature through a subject specialist's lens, with the accuracy and practical judgement that come from field knowledge; a scholarly review holds the same material to academic standards, for publication or thesis support."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Review for regulatory submission"}</b><span>{"Literature compiled and appraised to the expectations of a regulator rather than a journal — for clinical evaluation reports under EU MDR, for 510(k), PMA and CE marking, and for the literature sections of IND, NDA and CTD dossiers."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"Qualitative and mixed-methods synthesis"}</b><span>{"Qualitative findings integrated to produce understandings beyond what any single study reported, reported under ENTREQ, or combined with quantitative evidence in a convergent design."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Disease and therapeutic areas"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Reviews are built by subject-matter experts who can read the studies in them, across oncology — emerging trends, new chemotherapy agents, immunotherapy and targeted therapy — neurological disorders including Alzheimer's, Parkinson's and multiple sclerosis, infectious disease and immunology covering vaccines, antimicrobial resistance and immune response mechanisms, and across cardiology, endocrinology, respiratory medicine, public health, nutrition, medical devices, pharmacology and health economics. Where a question crosses fields, so does the team."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-who-we-serve-lifxp4"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who commissions a literature review."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Academics are only part of it. Most of these reviews exist because somebody has to justify a decision to a regulator, a payer or a panel."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Academic and research institutions"}</b><span>{"Dissertations, theses, topic mapping and gap analysis for grant applications and peer-reviewed publication — where an examiner will check the search before anything else."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Pharmaceutical and biotechnology companies"}</b><span>{"Mechanism-of-action reviews, safety and efficacy evaluations and the literature sections of regulatory dossiers, including IND, NDA and CTD submissions."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Medical device and diagnostic firms"}</b><span>{"Clinical evaluation reports for CE marking under EU MDR, and the literature behind 510(k) and PMA submissions, white papers and technical documentation."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Healthcare providers and clinicians"}</b><span>{"Structured synthesis of recent evidence for diagnostic and treatment decisions, CME content and practice guideline development — fitted around clinical work."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Hospitals and medical research units"}</b><span>{"Clinical audits, protocol development, ethics committee submissions and internal training material built on current findings rather than on what was taught."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Contract research organisations"}</b><span>{"Trial documentation, literature-based justification of endpoints, and the background sections of study protocols and investigator brochures."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "6" }}><b>{"HTA and market access teams"}</b><span>{"Comparative effectiveness and outcomes evidence, cost-effectiveness and value demonstration, and the literature behind payer submissions and value dossiers."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "7" }}><b>{"Regulatory and government agencies"}</b><span>{"Evidence gathering for public health programmes, the data reviews behind policy decisions, and the technical documentation that compliance and surveillance work demands."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why the destination changes the document"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"A thesis chapter is judged on whether the candidate can appraise; a grant background is judged on whether the gap is real and fundable; a clinical evaluation report is judged on whether the search was systematic enough to support a safety claim under EU MDR; and a journal review is judged on whether it adds something to a literature that already has several reviews in it. The same underlying search can serve all four, but the writing cannot — which is why we ask what it is for before asking what it is about."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-our-compliance-kqep5h"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and guideline standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The standards a review is written under."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Pubrica works in compliance with this guidance. Which one applies depends on the type of review, and choosing it at the start is what stops a rewrite later."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"PRISMA 2020 and PRISMA-ScR reporting guidelines"}>{"PRISMA"}<em>{"2020 · ScR"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(PRISMA 2020, PRISMA-ScR)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Systematic reviews report under PRISMA 2020; scoping reviews under PRISMA-ScR, which drops the risk-of-bias requirement but keeps the search and selection reporting. Narrative and conceptual reviews are not covered by either, and saying so honestly is better than implying a rigour the method does not have."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Cochrane Handbook and JBI methodology"}>{"Cochrane"}<em>{"JBI"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Cochrane Handbook and JBI methodology "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(Cochrane, JBI)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The conduct standards behind the reporting. Cochrane governs how a review of effectiveness is run; the JBI manual covers the review types Cochrane does not — scoping, umbrella, prevalence, qualitative and mixed-methods — and supplies the critical appraisal instruments that go with each."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"EQUATOR Network reporting guidelines"}>{"EQUATOR"}<em>{"network"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Enhancing the Quality and Transparency of Health Research "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(EQUATOR)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The index that decides which checklist your review belongs to, and the one most authors have never opened. MOOSE for observational synthesis, ENTREQ for qualitative, SWiM for narrative synthesis, PRISMA-S for the search itself. Journals increasingly require the right one as a submitted file."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"AMSTAR 2, GRADE, ROBIS and Newcastle-Ottawa Scale appraisal tools"}>{"AMSTAR 2"}<em>{"GRADE · NOS"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Appraisal and certainty instruments "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(AMSTAR 2, ROBIS 1.2, GRADE, NOS, JBI)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Each included study appraised with the instrument its design calls for — the Newcastle-Ottawa Scale or the JBI instruments for observational work, RoB 2 for trials — and the result recorded per domain rather than summarised as “high quality” or reduced to a single score, which is why summary scales such as Jadad are no longer used. AMSTAR 2 and ROBIS 1.2 then judge the review itself, and GRADE rates the certainty of what it concludes."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"PICO, PECO and PICOT question frameworks"}>{"PICO"}<em>{"PECO · PICOT"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Question and gap frameworks "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(PICO, PECO, PICOT, SPIDER)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The frameworks that turn a topic into a question, and then turn an absence into a stated gap. A gap expressed as PICO — this population, this exposure, this comparator, this outcome, unstudied — is something a committee can fund. The same gap expressed as a theme is something they can only agree with."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"ICMJE, CONSORT and the journal's own rules"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Authorship, competing interests, funding and any use of AI in searching or drafting are declared under ICMJE. Where a review summarises trials, CONSORT governs what those trials should have reported and therefore what you can legitimately extract from them. And on top of all of it sits the target journal's own guidance, which is where reviews most often come back from — a manuscript can satisfy every international standard and still be returned for a reference style. Our literature review help builds to the journal alongside the guideline, not after it."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Two people read every study that makes it in."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Pubrica measures this by which decisions a tool is allowed to make, not by how much of the reading it can do. Every study that makes it in is read by two people, and the reader of your review is told where a tool was used."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Prioritisation — ranking records so the likely includes surface first, which cuts title and abstract time substantially and is well established in the methods literature. Deduplication. Flagging where a reported outcome does not match the protocol."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Unsupervised include or exclude decisions; extraction accepted without a human check; appraisal judgements; and anything on a review headed for a regulatory or health technology assessment submission, where an assessor traces every judgement to a person."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as a research integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-how-it-works-1xe12xi"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How our literature review and gap analysis service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Our step-by-step process."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six stages. The fifth is the one you are paying for; the four before it are what make it defensible."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step one"}</span> <h3>{"Objectives, scope and protocol"}</h3> <p>{"What the review is for decides what it has to be. A thesis chapter, a grant background section, a clinical evaluation report for a regulator and a journal article are four different documents, and the audience — examiner, funding committee, notified body, editor — sets the standard. From that we choose the review type deliberately — systematic, scoping, targeted, umbrella, narrative or integrative — and fix the databases, the inclusion and exclusion criteria and the search vocabulary before any reading begins. Choosing the type afterwards is the most common reason a review has to be restarted."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step two"}</span> <h3>{"Comprehensive literature search"}</h3> <p>{"Run across PubMed and MEDLINE, Embase, the Cochrane Library, Scopus, Web of Science and CINAHL, with the subject databases the question needs, plus grey literature, clinical guidelines, trial registries and regulatory documents where they bear on it. The strategy is written down line by line and handed to you, dated and reproducible, so the review can be updated rather than repeated."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step three"}</span> <h3>{"Screening and selection"}</h3> <p>{"Records deduplicated in EndNote or Zotero, then screened on title and abstract against the pre-set criteria, and full texts assessed the same way. Reported under PRISMA or its equivalent, with a flow diagram whose numbers reconcile and a record of why each full text was excluded — a list that cannot be reconstructed afterwards."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step four"}</span> <h3>{"Critical appraisal and data extraction"}</h3> <p>{"Each study appraised with a named instrument — AMSTAR 2, GRADE, the Newcastle-Ottawa Scale or the JBI instruments — and the data extracted into a structured review matrix rather than summarised in prose: design, setting, population, exposure, comparator, outcomes, effect estimates, funding, limitations. The matrix is what makes the next step possible, and you get it as a working file."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step five"}</span> <h3>{"Gap analysis and insight generation"}</h3> <p>{"The evidence mapped by population and outcome, then read for four things: where there is nothing, where there is only weak evidence, where the studies contradict each other, and which group has been excluded from all of it. Each gap is written as a specific question in PICO or PECO terms, with the study design that would answer it — which is what turns a review into the first section of a proposal."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step six"}</span> <h3>{"Drafting, revision and delivery"}</h3> <p>{"Written to the structure the destination requires — PRISMA for a systematic review, the funder’s template for a proposal, MDR expectations for a clinical evaluation report, the journal’s own guidance for a publication — with evidence tables, the review matrix, the flow diagram and references in your style. Then you read it, argue with it, and we revise until it is right, with no cap on rounds inside the scope agreed."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} style={{ borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)", background: "var(--paper-2)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send the topic. We will tell you whether there is a gap."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"A scoping search costs nothing and answers the question worth answering first: has this review been published already, is there enough literature to review, and is there a gap specific enough to build a proposal on. We would rather tell you in week one than after you have written the background section."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What the quote is built on"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Review type"}</b><span>{"Narrative, scoping, targeted or systematic"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Destination"}</b><span>{"Thesis, proposal, journal or dossier"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Databases"}</b><span>{"How many the question needs"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Volume"}</b><span>{"Records returned and screened"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Appraisal"}</b><span>{"Whether each study is graded"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Gap output"}</b><span>{"Narrative, matrix or full evidence map"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"The biggest single driver is the review type, and it is worth getting right rather than getting cheap: a narrative review costs a fraction of a systematic one and will not satisfy an examiner who asked for a systematic one. We will say which your purpose actually requires, including when the answer is the less expensive option."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"The evidence gap map"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"“More research is needed” is not a gap."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A gap analysis has to name which population, which outcome, and what study would close it. This is what that looks like when it is done properly — click any cell. Where the map itself is the deliverable rather than a section of a review, that is an "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/research-services/evidence-gap-map/"}>{"evidence gap map"}</a>{", built for funders and portfolio teams."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"egm rv rv-d1"} data-egm={""}> <div className={"egm__bar"}> <span><b>{"Read the map."}</b>{" The filled cells are what exists. The empty ones are the argument."}</span> <span data-egm-frame={""}>{"5 populations × 5 outcome domains · mapped from one systematic search"}</span> </div> <div className={"egm__top"} data-egm-top={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"egm__q"} data-topic={"dm"} aria-pressed={"true"}> <b>{"Worked example one"}</b><span>{"Digital self-management interventions in type 2 diabetes"}</span> </button> <button type={"button"} className={"egm__q"} data-topic={"str"} aria-pressed={"false"}> <b>{"Worked example two"}</b><span>{"Machine-learning triage of imaging in acute stroke"}</span> </button> </div> <div className={"egm__sum"} data-egm-sum={""}><button type={"button"} className={"egm__s"} data-f={"all"} aria-pressed={"true"}><b>{"179"}</b><span>{"Studies mapped in the search"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__s"} data-f={"none"} aria-pressed={"false"}><b>{"5"}</b><span>{"Cells with no evidence at all"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__s"} data-f={"weak"} aria-pressed={"false"}><b>{"7"}</b><span>{"Cells carried by weak designs only"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__s"} data-f={"conflict"} aria-pressed={"false"}><b>{"2"}</b><span>{"Cells where the studies disagree"}</span></button></div> <div className={"egm__in"}> <div className={"egm__map"} data-egm-map={""}><div className={"egm__grid"} style={{ '--cols': "minmax(104px,1.1fr) repeat(5, minmax(76px,1fr))" }} role={"grid"}><div className={"egm__hrow"} role={"row"}><span className={"egm__corner"}>{"Population ↓ / Outcome →"}</span><span className={"egm__ch"}>{"Glycaemic control"}</span><span className={"egm__ch"}>{"Adherence"}</span><span className={"egm__ch"}>{"Quality of life"}</span><span className={"egm__ch"}>{"Cost-effectiveness"}</span><span className={"egm__ch"}>{"Equity of access"}</span></div><div className={"egm__row"} role={"row"}><span className={"egm__rh"}>{"Adults 18–64"}</span><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--rich is-on"} data-r={"0"} data-c={"0"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Adults 18–64, Glycaemic control: 41 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "42px", height: "42px" }}>{"41"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--rich"} data-r={"0"} data-c={"1"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Adults 18–64, Adherence: 23 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "37px", height: "37px" }}>{"23"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--rich"} data-r={"0"} data-c={"2"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Adults 18–64, Quality of life: 17 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "35px", height: "35px" }}>{"17"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--some"} data-r={"0"} data-c={"3"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Adults 18–64, Cost-effectiveness: 6 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "31px", height: "31px" }}>{"6"}</span><i className={"egm__f egm__f--weak"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"◐"}</i></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--some"} data-r={"0"} data-c={"4"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Adults 18–64, Equity of access: 4 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "30px", height: "30px" }}>{"4"}</span><i className={"egm__f egm__f--weak"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"◐"}</i></button></div><div className={"egm__row"} role={"row"}><span className={"egm__rh"}>{"Older adults 65+"}</span><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--rich"} data-r={"1"} data-c={"0"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Older adults 65+, Glycaemic control: 14 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "34px", height: "34px" }}>{"14"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--rich"} data-r={"1"} data-c={"1"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Older adults 65+, Adherence: 9 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "32px", height: "32px" }}>{"9"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--rich"} data-r={"1"} data-c={"2"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Older adults 65+, Quality of life: 8 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "32px", height: "32px" }}>{"8"}</span><i className={"egm__f egm__f--conflict"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"!"}</i></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--thin"} data-r={"1"} data-c={"3"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Older adults 65+, Cost-effectiveness: 2 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "28px", height: "28px" }}>{"2"}</span><i className={"egm__f egm__f--weak"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"◐"}</i></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--none"} data-r={"1"} data-c={"4"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Older adults 65+, Equity of access: no studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "26px", height: "26px" }}>{"—"}</span></button></div><div className={"egm__row"} role={"row"}><span className={"egm__rh"}>{"Multimorbidity"}</span><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--rich"} data-r={"2"} data-c={"0"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Multimorbidity, Glycaemic control: 11 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "33px", height: "33px" }}>{"11"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--some"} data-r={"2"} data-c={"1"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Multimorbidity, Adherence: 5 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "30px", height: "30px" }}>{"5"}</span><i className={"egm__f egm__f--weak"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"◐"}</i></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--some"} data-r={"2"} data-c={"2"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Multimorbidity, Quality of life: 6 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "31px", height: "31px" }}>{"6"}</span><i className={"egm__f egm__f--conflict"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"!"}</i></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--thin"} data-r={"2"} data-c={"3"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Multimorbidity, Cost-effectiveness: 1 study"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "27px", height: "27px" }}>{"1"}</span><i className={"egm__f egm__f--weak"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"◐"}</i></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--none"} data-r={"2"} data-c={"4"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Multimorbidity, Equity of access: no studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "26px", height: "26px" }}>{"—"}</span></button></div><div className={"egm__row"} role={"row"}><span className={"egm__rh"}>{"Low-resource settings"}</span><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--rich"} data-r={"3"} data-c={"0"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Low-resource settings, Glycaemic control: 9 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "32px", height: "32px" }}>{"9"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--some"} data-r={"3"} data-c={"1"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Low-resource settings, Adherence: 3 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "29px", height: "29px" }}>{"3"}</span><i className={"egm__f egm__f--weak"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"◐"}</i></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--thin"} data-r={"3"} data-c={"2"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Low-resource settings, Quality of life: 2 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "28px", height: "28px" }}>{"2"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--none"} data-r={"3"} data-c={"3"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Low-resource settings, Cost-effectiveness: no studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "26px", height: "26px" }}>{"—"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--some"} data-r={"3"} data-c={"4"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Low-resource settings, Equity of access: 7 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "31px", height: "31px" }}>{"7"}</span></button></div><div className={"egm__row"} role={"row"}><span className={"egm__rh"}>{"Pregnancy and GDM"}</span><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--some"} data-r={"4"} data-c={"0"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Pregnancy and GDM, Glycaemic control: 6 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "31px", height: "31px" }}>{"6"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--some"} data-r={"4"} data-c={"1"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Pregnancy and GDM, Adherence: 4 studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "30px", height: "30px" }}>{"4"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--thin"} data-r={"4"} data-c={"2"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Pregnancy and GDM, Quality of life: 1 study"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "27px", height: "27px" }}>{"1"}</span><i className={"egm__f egm__f--weak"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"◐"}</i></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--none"} data-r={"4"} data-c={"3"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Pregnancy and GDM, Cost-effectiveness: no studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "26px", height: "26px" }}>{"—"}</span></button><button type={"button"} className={"egm__c egm__c--none"} data-r={"4"} data-c={"4"} role={"gridcell"} aria-label={"Pregnancy and GDM, Equity of access: no studies"}><span className={"egm__b"} style={{ width: "26px", height: "26px" }}>{"—"}</span></button></div></div><p className={"egm__key"}><span><i className={"k-rich"} />{"8 or more studies"}</span><span><i className={"k-some"} />{"3 to 7"}</span><span><i className={"k-thin"} />{"1 to 2"}</span><span><i className={"k-none"} />{"No evidence"}</span><span><i className={"k-weak"} />{"Weak designs only"}</span><span><i className={"k-conf"} />{"Studies disagree"}</span></p></div> <div className={"egm__side"} data-egm-side={""}><p className={"egm__lab"}>{"Selected cell"}</p><p className={"egm__cell"}>{"Adults 18–64 × Glycaemic control"}</p><p className={"egm__meta"}>{"41 studies found · Digital self-management interventions in type 2 diabetes"}</p><p className={"egm__h"}>{"What the evidence is"}</p><div className={"egm__des"}><div className={"egm__d"}>{"Randomised"}<b>{"28"}</b></div><div className={"egm__d"}>{"Observational"}<b>{"13"}</b></div><div className={"egm__d"}>{"Total"}<b>{"41"}</b></div></div><p className={"egm__t"}>{"Well covered. Randomised evidence is consistent in direction, and the pooled effect on HbA1c is the most secure finding on this map."}</p><p className={"egm__h"}>{"On this map"}</p><p className={"egm__t"}>{"Twenty-five cells, five of them empty. "}<b>{"The empty cells are the deliverable"}</b>{" — they are where a funder will believe you when you say the work has not been done. Notice the shape as well as the holes: the evidence thins out from left to right, so the outcomes that decide whether a programme gets adopted are the ones least studied."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"egm__foot"}><b>{"A worked example built on the shape of two real reviews."}</b>{" Study counts are illustrative; what is not illustrative is the pattern. Evidence clusters where it is easy to collect and thins out exactly where a decision has to be made — in the harder populations, on the outcomes that cost money, and in the settings that were never the ones doing the research."}</p> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Four kinds of gap, and only one of them is an empty cell"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Use the four tallies above the map as filters. An "}<b>{"evidence gap"}</b>{" is a cell with nothing in it. A "}<b>{"methodological gap"}</b>{" is a cell full of studies that cannot support the claims made from them — retrospective where prospective was needed, surrogate outcomes standing in for real ones, validation on the data the model was trained against. A "}<b>{"contradiction"}</b>{" is a cell where the studies disagree, which is usually the most publishable gap of all, because nobody has to be persuaded the question matters. And a "}<b>{"population gap"}</b>{" is the row that is thin all the way across: the group everyone excluded, for reasons that made each study easier and the literature as a whole less useful. A review that reports only the first kind has done a quarter of the work."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-our-experts-f0g9ov"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, the handover says which of them did which stage, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible, so a reviewer, an editor or an assessor can run it again."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Question, scope, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, PRISMA"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"RoB 2, ROBINS-I, QUADAS-3, JBI"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, CONSORT"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-sample-work-3jekwr"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What the handover contains."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Every Pubrica review returns the search that found the literature, the matrix that organises it and the gap statements that come out of it — not only the prose. Use the tabs to see each one."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Literature review and gap analysis"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"Scoping review · 179 studies mapped · 5 gaps stated"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"6 databases · PRISMA-ScR · review matrix and evidence gap map supplied"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the literature review handover"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"lr-t1"} aria-controls={"lr-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"Scope"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"lr-t2"} aria-controls={"lr-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"Matrix"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"lr-t3"} aria-controls={"lr-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"Gaps"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"lr-t4"} aria-controls={"lr-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"Files"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"lr-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"lr-t1"}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Review type"}</dt><dd>{"Scoping review, reported under PRISMA-ScR"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Purpose"}</dt><dd>{"Background and justification for a five-year programme grant"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Framework"}</dt><dd>{"PECO, with the population axis pre-specified for the map"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Databases"}</dt><dd>{"PubMed, Embase, Cochrane Library, Scopus, Web of Science, CINAHL"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Grey literature"}</dt><dd>{"Trial registries, HTA reports and two national guideline bodies"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Limits"}</dt><dd>{"2015 onwards, declared and justified; no language restriction"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Appraisal"}</dt><dd>{"Design recorded for every study; formal appraisal on the 38 that carry a claim"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Output"}</dt><dd>{"Narrative synthesis, review matrix, evidence gap map, five gap statements"}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"lr-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"lr-t2"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"One row per study, not one paragraph"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"179 rows, each carrying design, setting, country, population, exposure, comparator, outcomes measured, effect estimate where reported, funding source and stated limitations."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Outcomes coded to a shared vocabulary"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Eleven different quality-of-life instruments collapsed onto one axis, with the original instrument retained in its own column so nothing is lost by the coding."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Population coded for the map"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Age band, comorbidity, setting and income classification captured for every study, which is what makes the population rows in the gap map possible rather than impressionistic."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Flagged during extraction"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Nine studies report a population in the abstract that the methods section does not support — most often “older adults” for a sample with a mean age of 61. Coded on the methods, with the discrepancy noted."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Queried with you"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Four studies are the same cohort reported four times. Counted once in the map and listed as four references, because a map that counts them separately overstates the evidence by exactly that much."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"179 studies · supplied as a spreadsheet you keep"}</span><span>{"Extendable, not a screenshot"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"lr-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"lr-t3"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"1"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Evidence gap · equity of access in older adults"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"No study measures whether these interventions widen or narrow access among people over 65. "}<b>{"What would close it:"}</b>{" a cohort with digital literacy and device access measured at baseline and outcomes reported by that stratum, not adjusted for it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"2"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Evidence gap · cost-effectiveness in low-resource settings"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Four effectiveness trials, no economic evaluation — in the setting where cost decides adoption. "}<b>{"What would close it:"}</b>{" a trial-based economic evaluation alongside an existing trial, using local unit costs rather than transferred ones."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"3"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Methodological gap · cost-effectiveness generally"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Six studies exist; five are modelled analyses resting on assumptions the trials never tested. There is literature here, and there is not yet evidence. "}<b>{"What would close it:"}</b>{" within-trial economic evaluation rather than another model."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"4"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Contradiction · quality of life in older adults"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Two trials report opposite directions of effect on wellbeing, and neither cites the other. "}<b>{"What would close it:"}</b>{" a trial powered for quality of life as a primary outcome, using one validated instrument."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"5"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Population gap · multimorbidity"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Thin across every outcome, because most studies exclude people on multiple medicines — a decision that made each study cleaner and the literature as a whole less useful. "}<b>{"What would close it:"}</b>{" a pragmatic trial that makes polypharmacy an inclusion criterion instead of an exclusion."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Each gap written in PECO terms, with a study design"}</span><span>{"Drafted as proposal text"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"lr-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"lr-t4"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The review"}</dt><dd>{"Narrative synthesis, structured by theme, formatted to the funder's template"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Search strategy"}</dt><dd>{"Line by line for every database, with counts and the date run"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Flow diagram"}</dt><dd>{"PRISMA-ScR, as an editable figure"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Review matrix"}</dt><dd>{"The full extraction spreadsheet, 179 rows, yours to extend"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Evidence tables"}</dt><dd>{"Grouped by theme, formatted for direct insertion"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Gap map"}</dt><dd>{"The population-by-outcome matrix as a figure and as data"}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Reference library"}</dt><dd>{"EndNote, Mendeley or Zotero, deduplicated and styled"}</dd></dl> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · client and topic details changed"}</span><span data-docpage={""}>{"Page 1 of 4"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"The handover is the review and the working documents that justify it. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each part."}</b></p> <p><b>{"The review matrix"}</b>{" is the part authors underestimate and then rely on most. Two hundred studies summarised in prose cannot be re-sorted, re-grouped or extended; two hundred rows in a spreadsheet can, which is why the same matrix usually survives into the thesis, the paper and the next grant."}</p> <p><b>{"The gap statements"}</b>{" are written as proposal text, not as findings. Each one names a population, an outcome and a study design, because that is what a funding committee can assess — and because “further research is warranted” has never persuaded anybody of anything."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Review type chosen first"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"From what the review has to survive, not from what is quickest."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Appraised, not just counted"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Every study judged with a named instrument, recorded per study."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Gaps named specifically"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Population, outcome and the design that would close it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"The matrix is yours"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"A working spreadsheet, extendable, not an appendix of screenshots."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a handover built round a review like yours — same review type, same field, same destination."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-lr"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-lr"}>{"Read the full handover"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-lr"}> <span><b>{"Read the full sample handover"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — scope, search, review matrix, the gap map and the five gap statements"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-lr"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Literature review and gap analysis · redacted sample"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Scoping review · 179 studies mapped · 5 gaps stated"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"6 databases · PRISMA-ScR · written as the background to a programme grant. Client names, journal names and identifying particulars have been removed or changed. Ask us and we will send one built around a review like yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"Scope, as agreed before searching"}</h4> <p>{"The review type was chosen from what the document had to survive. This one is the background section of a five-year programme grant, so the panel is assessing whether the gap is real and fundable rather than whether the synthesis is exhaustive — which makes a scoping review with a strong gap analysis the right instrument, and a full systematic review an expensive way to answer a different question."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Element"}</th><th>{"As agreed"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Review type"}</td><td>{"Scoping review, reported under PRISMA-ScR"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Purpose"}</td><td>{"Background and justification for a programme grant application"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Framework"}</td><td>{"PECO, with the population axis pre-specified so the map could be built"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Databases"}</td><td>{"PubMed, Embase, Cochrane Library, Scopus, Web of Science, CINAHL"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Grey literature"}</td><td>{"Trial registries, two HTA bodies and two national guideline producers"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Limits"}</td><td>{"2015 onwards, justified by a change in the standard of care; no language restriction"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Appraisal"}</td><td>{"Design recorded for all 179; formal appraisal on the 38 carrying a claim"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Output"}</td><td>{"Narrative synthesis, review matrix, evidence gap map, five gap statements"}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"Search and selection"}</h4> <p>{"The strategy is supplied line by line for each database with the count it returned and the date it was run, so the review can be updated rather than repeated when the grant is resubmitted."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Stage"}</th><th>{"n"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Records identified from databases"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"3,912"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Records from registries, HTA reports and guidelines"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"147"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Records from citation searching in both directions"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"88"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Duplicates removed"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"1,402"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Records screened on title and abstract"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"2,745"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Records excluded at screening"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"2,438"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Full texts assessed"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"307"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Full texts excluded, with reasons recorded"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"128"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Studies included in the map"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"179"}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Four reports were found to describe the same cohort. They are counted once in the map and listed as four references, because counting them separately overstates the evidence by exactly that much."}</p> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"The review matrix"}</h4> <p>{"One row per study rather than one paragraph. This is the file clients keep using after the document is finished, because a matrix can be re-sorted, re-grouped and extended, and two hundred studies summarised in prose cannot."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Column"}</th><th>{"What it holds"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Design"}</td><td>{"Randomised, prospective, retrospective, qualitative, modelled"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Setting and country"}</td><td>{"Including income classification, which the map's rows depend on"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Population"}</td><td>{"Age band, comorbidity and recruitment route, coded from the methods"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Exposure and comparator"}</td><td>{"As described, with the intervention's actual content rather than its label"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Outcomes measured"}</td><td>{"Coded to a shared vocabulary, with the original instrument kept alongside"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Effect estimate"}</td><td>{"Where reported, with its interval and the source page"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Appraisal"}</td><td>{"Instrument used and judgement reached, per study"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Funding and limitations"}</td><td>{"As stated by the authors, and what they did not state"}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__cl"}><b>{"Flagged during extraction."}</b>{" Nine studies describe a population in the abstract that the methods section does not support — most often “older adults” for a sample with a mean age of 61. Every study is coded on its methods, not its abstract, and the discrepancies are listed. This is the kind of thing that only surfaces when someone reads the full text, and it is why a map built from abstracts is not worth building."}</p> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"The evidence gap map"}</h4> <p>{"Five populations against five outcome domains, twenty-five cells. Five are empty, seven are carried entirely by designs too weak to support the claims made from them, and two contain studies that contradict each other. The map is supplied as a figure and as data."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Finding"}</th><th>{"Cells"}</th><th>{"What it means for the proposal"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"No evidence at all"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"5"}</td><td>{"The strongest claim available, and the one a panel can verify"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Weak designs only"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"7"}</td><td>{"Literature exists; evidence does not. A different argument, equally fundable"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Studies disagree"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"2"}</td><td>{"Nobody has to be persuaded the question matters"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Thin across a whole row"}</td><td className={"num"}>{"1"}</td><td>{"A population systematically excluded, which is a finding in itself"}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"The five gap statements"}</h4> <p>{"Written as proposal text rather than as findings. Each names a population, an outcome and the study design that would close it, because that is what a committee can assess."}</p> <ul> <li><b>{"Equity of access in older adults."}</b>{" No study measures whether these interventions widen or narrow access among people over 65. Closed by a cohort with digital literacy and device access measured at baseline, and outcomes reported by that stratum rather than adjusted for it."}</li> <li><b>{"Cost-effectiveness in low-resource settings."}</b>{" Four effectiveness trials, no economic evaluation — in the setting where cost decides adoption. Closed by a trial-based economic evaluation alongside an existing trial, using local unit costs rather than transferred ones."}</li> <li><b>{"Cost-effectiveness generally — a methodological gap."}</b>{" Six studies exist; five are modelled analyses resting on assumptions the trials never tested. Closed by a within-trial evaluation rather than another model."}</li> <li><b>{"Quality of life in older adults — a contradiction."}</b>{" Two trials report opposite directions of effect, and neither cites the other. Closed by a trial powered for quality of life as a primary outcome, using one validated instrument."}</li> <li><b>{"Multimorbidity — a population gap."}</b>{" Thin across every outcome, because most studies exclude people on multiple medicines. Closed by a pragmatic trial that makes polypharmacy an inclusion criterion rather than an exclusion."}</li> </ul> <h4><span>{"6"}</span>{"What is handed over"}</h4> <ul> <li>{"The review itself, structured by theme and formatted to the funder’s template."}</li> <li>{"The search strategy for every database, line by line, with counts and dates."}</li> <li>{"The PRISMA-ScR flow diagram as an editable figure."}</li> <li>{"The full review matrix, 179 rows, as a spreadsheet you keep and can extend."}</li> <li>{"Evidence tables grouped by theme, formatted for direct insertion."}</li> <li>{"The evidence gap map as a figure and as the underlying data."}</li> <li>{"A deduplicated reference library in EndNote, Mendeley or Zotero, styled to your format."}</li> </ul> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Pubrica supports the work; authorship remains yours. Where our contribution should be acknowledged under ICMJE, the handover drafts the wording for you to approve, and any AI-assisted searching or drafting is declared in the methods."}</p> <div className={"fsm__end"}> <p>{"Prepared by Pubrica. Pubrica is a trading name of Guires"}<sup className={"reg"}>{"®"}</sup>{", registered in England, Wales and India."}</p> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/downloads/pubrica-literature-review-sample.pdf"} download={""}>{"Download this as a PDF"}</a> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"ba rv"}> <div className={"ba__hd"}><span><b>{"Before and after"}</b>{" · the gap statement from one review, redacted"}</span><span>{"Rehabilitation · thesis chapter"}</span></div> <div className={"ba__g"}> <div className={"ba__c ba__c--b"}> <p className={"ba__k"}>{"As it arrived"}</p> <p className={"ba__t"}>{"Few studies have examined this area, and further research is needed to clarify the relationship."}</p> <ul className={"ba__f"}><li><span>{"“Few” is not a number, so the claim cannot be checked or contradicted."}</span></li><li><span>{"“Further research is needed” appears in most papers ever written and commits to nothing."}</span></li><li><span>{"It gives an examiner or a funding panel nothing to agree with."}</span></li><li><span>{"It does not say what the next study should do, which is the whole purpose of a gap statement."}</span></li></ul> </div> <div className={"ba__c ba__c--a"}> <p className={"ba__k"}>{"As it went out"}</p> <p className={"ba__t"}>{"Eleven studies have examined this relationship in this population since 2015. Nine were cross-sectional; of the two cohorts, one followed participants for six weeks. None measured the outcome beyond discharge and none reported results for the subgroup that carries the highest baseline risk. The gap is therefore not that the area is unstudied. It is that no study has followed the outcome long enough to see whether the early difference persists."}</p> <ul className={"ba__f"}><li><span>{"Counted, so it is falsifiable. If a twelfth study exists, someone can say so."}</span></li><li><span>{"The design breakdown shows why the existing evidence cannot answer the question."}</span></li><li><span>{"The gap is specific enough that the next study follows from it."}</span></li><li><span>{"It gives a reviewer something to agree with rather than something to skim."}</span></li></ul> </div> </div> <p className={"ba__foot"}><b>{"A gap statement is a claim about the literature, and a claim needs a count."}</b>{" The version on the right took no longer to write — it took a search that had already been done properly, and an extraction matrix that recorded design and follow-up rather than conclusions."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Benefits of our literature review services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What it gives you."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Mostly time. But the thing you cannot buy back is the year spent answering a question somebody published while you were writing the proposal."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"bens rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"01"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"A proposal that names its gap"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Funding committees do not reject proposals for being uninteresting; they reject them for not establishing that the work has not already been done. A gap stated as a population, an outcome and the study design that would close it is an argument a panel can score. A paragraph ending “further research is needed” is not."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"02"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The months back"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"A thorough review is four to six weeks of reading that most researchers do not have and cannot delegate to anyone without domain knowledge. Buying it back is the whole reason this service exists, and it is why clinicians and time-poor academics are most of who uses it."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"03"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Twenty years of Pubrica domain expertise"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The review is built by people who can read the studies in it — clinicians, epidemiologists and life-science PhDs working across oncology, neurology, infectious disease, cardiology, nutrition, medical devices and health economics. Knowing which finding is load-bearing is not something a search tool does."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"04"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Work that has a second life"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The search strategy, the reference library and the review matrix outlive the document they were built for. The same three files become the thesis chapter, the paper's introduction, the next grant's background section, the systematic review two years later, and the update when a reviewer asks whether the search is current."}</span></span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-packages-1oyqjie"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three ways in, depending on what the review has to survive."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Tailored to the stage you are at and the standard your destination sets. Every package is run by a subject expert with a dedicated project coordinator, and every one hands over the search and the matrix, not only the prose."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"trn rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"trn__i"}><p className={"trn__k"}>{"Rush"}</p><p className={"trn__v"}>{"1 week"}</p><p className={"trn__d"}>{"Where capacity allows. Quoted on capacity rather than on urgency, so a rush is not a surcharge for your deadline."}</p></div> <div className={"trn__i"}><p className={"trn__k"}>{"Standard"}</p><p className={"trn__v"}>{"2–3 weeks"}</p><p className={"trn__d"}>{"The normal route, and the one that leaves room for a revision round before your own deadline."}</p></div> <div className={"trn__i"}><p className={"trn__k"}>{"Extended"}</p><p className={"trn__v"}>{"4–5 weeks"}</p><p className={"trn__d"}>{"Larger scopes, multi-database searches, and anything needing a second reviewer throughout."}</p></div> </div> <div className={"tiers rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Basic"}</span> <h3>{"Literature mapping"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Early-stage research and academic assignments — where you need to know what is out there before committing to anything"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $340"}</b><span>{"up to 40 sources · 2 databases"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"7–10 working days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Structured overview of the relevant studies"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Major themes and trends identified and grouped"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"High-level gap identification"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Reference library in APA, MLA or Vancouver"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Search strategy handed over, so it can be extended later"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: critical appraisal; PRISMA reporting; the full gap map."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-lr"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-lr"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Basic"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Advanced"}</span> <h3>{"Critical review and gap analysis"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Research proposals, theses and grant applications — where the gap has to convince somebody who can say no"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $620"}</b><span>{"up to 80 sources · an appraisal instrument per study"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"10–15 working days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Comprehensive synthesis across the databases the question needs"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"In-depth critical appraisal of each study, with a named instrument"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Structured gap identification in PICO or PECO terms"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Review matrix and evidence tables, supplied as working files"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Evidence gap map across populations and outcomes"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Reported to PRISMA or the equivalent for the review type"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: dual screening; full systematic method; journal formatting."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-lr"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-lr"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Advanced"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Premium"}</span> <h3>{"Publication-ready systematic review"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Journal publication, clinical trial support and regulatory submissions — where the method itself will be audited"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $820"}</b><span>{"up to 120 sources · PROSPERO and grey literature quoted separately"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"15–20 working days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A full systematic review, reported to PRISMA throughout"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Protocol development and a reproducible database search strategy"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Dual independent screening and quality appraisal — AMSTAR 2, GRADE"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Detailed gap analysis with visual evidence mapping"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Journal-specific formatting and editorial support"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Submission support and response to reviewer comments"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: meta-analysis; PROSPERO registration; a living update schedule."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-lr"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-lr"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Premium"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"psv rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"A screened reference set"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"40–60"}</b><span>{"papers, screened"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"With the ones rejected, and why"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Not a search export. Every paper read against stated criteria, the includes and the excludes both listed, and the exclusion reason given for each — because the rejected set is what a reviewer checks to see whether their own paper was missed or considered."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"A review matrix"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"One table"}</b><span>{"every paper, every field"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Design, population, outcome, finding, limitation"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"The extraction table the review is written from, handed over rather than kept. It is what makes the synthesis checkable, and it is the thing you will reuse when the next paper needs the same background."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"What lands"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"Named gaps"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"Each one"}</b><span>{"with the study that closes it"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Not “further research is needed”"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Every gap stated as a specific deficiency — in data type, sample size, population or geography — with the design that would close it. A gap a reviewer can verify is worth more than a gap you assert."}</p> </div> <p className={"psv__foot"}><b>{"The reference count is a range because it is set by the question, not by the package."}</b>{" A narrow clinical question may be answered properly by thirty papers and a broad one may need ninety. We tell you the expected range at scoping and report the actual number with the reasons it differed."}</p> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"Rewriting an existing review is quoted separately and starts with a written critique rather than a revision, because it has to say honestly whether the problem is repairable. Structure, synthesis, appraisal and referencing can all be fixed after the fact. A search that covered one database cannot — it has to be re-run and re-screened, and a rewrite that pretends otherwise will fail at the same point with the next reader. We will tell you which of the two you have before you commit."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-guarantee-a6py6n"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A gap analysis can only report what the literature contains. Here are the terms before you commit to anything."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"No refunds, because a refund does not get your proposal funded or your review published — it just ends the relationship with the problem still on your desk. What we offer instead is the thing that actually helps: we keep working on it."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Unlimited revisions, within the agreed scope"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"No cap on rounds and no clock on them inside the scope agreed. If the structure is wrong or the synthesis does not land, we do it again."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A missed database, a study misclassified, a reference wrongly formatted — if the work comes back because of something we ran or wrote, correcting it is free."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Delivered on the date agreed"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"We quote a date we can meet and we meet it. If a deadline is genuinely at risk you hear it from us early, not on the day."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Your decisions stay yours"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"We advise on the review type, the scope and which gap is worth pursuing, argue a view and tell you plainly when we disagree. What goes in your name is settled by you, every time."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"05"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Mutual NDA on request"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Signed before you send anything, in both directions, at no cost. Your question, your data and the fact that you are working with us stay confidential either way — and we will sign yours rather than insisting on ours."}</p></div> </div> <div className={"rate rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"rate__score"}> <b>{"9.4"}</b><span>{"/10"}</span> </div> <div className={"rate__body"}> <p className={"rate__t"}><span className={"rate__stars"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"★★★★★"}</span>{" Average client rating"}</p> <p className={"rate__d"}>{"From "}<b>{"3,000 responses"}</b>{" to Pubrica’s own post-delivery survey, sent to every client at handover, January 2024 to June 2026. It is our figure, from our records, and we say so rather than borrowing a badge."}</p> </div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" We cannot guarantee that a gap exists. Sometimes the honest finding is that your question was answered two years ago in a journal outside your usual reading, and we will tell you that in week one rather than build a review around pretending otherwise — it is the most valuable thing this service does, and the least welcome. We also cannot guarantee funding or acceptance; those decisions belong to a committee and an editor. Unlimited revision covers the review we were engaged to write; a changed question or a second review is new work."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"A free scoping search first"}</p> <p>{"Before you commit to anything, we run the check that decides whether the project should exist: has this review been published or registered already, is there enough literature to review, and is there a gap narrow enough to build on. It costs nothing, and it is the cheapest week you will spend on the whole project."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"The search and the matrix are yours"}</p> <p>{"The strategy line by line with the counts and dates, the deduplicated reference library, and the full extraction spreadsheet. A review you cannot re-run is a review you cannot update, and those files should not sit with your supplier — they are the part that keeps working after the document is finished."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"GDPR and data privacy"}</p> <p>{"Pubrica works with researchers in India, across the United Kingdom and Europe, in North America, throughout Asia-Pacific and the Middle East, and in Africa and Latin America, and every project is handled the same way wherever it comes from. Your topic, your unpublished proposal and your draft are held under GDPR, kept only as long as the project needs them, never used to train anything, and never shared outside your project team."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"No ghost authorship"}</p> <p>{"We search, appraise and write. We do not become an undeclared author. Where Pubrica's involvement should be acknowledged under ICMJE or GPP, we say so and draft the wording for you to approve, and any AI-assisted searching or drafting is declared in the methods."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-client-stories-1ew26zu"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three reviews, and what each one unlocked."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named author has confirmed it in writing."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Author testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“The review was methodologically sound and well written, but what mattered was the gap analysis — it named research areas we had walked past. It shaped the grant proposal, and the work behind it carried through to publication.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"RESEARCH"}<br />{"METHODOLOGY"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Methods"}<br />{"& Evidence"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Dr A. Mehta"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Academic researcher · India"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"JIF —"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“We had a deadline that should not have been possible. The structuring and synthesis are what made it work — not speed for its own sake, but knowing which of two hundred papers actually had to be read closely.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--a"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"CLINICAL"}<br />{"EPIDEMIOLOGY"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Evidence"}<br />{"Synthesis"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Dr Claire Thompson"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Clinical researcher · United Kingdom"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"JIF —"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“Their approach to identifying gaps changed our study objectives, not just our introduction. We narrowed the question considerably on the strength of it, and the paper was the better for it.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"LIFE"}<br />{"SCIENCES"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Research"}<br />{"& Practice"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Prof. K. Ramasamy"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— PhD supervisor · Life sciences, India"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"JIF —"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""}><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot is-on"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 1"} /><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 2"} /></div> <div className={"tcar__btns"}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-literature-review-faq-qw26fx"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Literature review and gap analysis FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Ten questions researchers ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure which type of review your purpose calls for, or whether your topic still has a gap in it? "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-0"}><span>{"How should a literature review be structured?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Thematically, and almost never chronologically. The structure that fails is the one that mirrors the order you read things in — a paragraph per study, each beginning with an author's name. The structure that works groups the literature into the three to six themes the field actually argues about, and within each theme states what is agreed, what is disputed, what the evidence rests on and where it stops. Every section should end by connecting back to your own objectives, so that by the closing paragraph the gap has already been demonstrated rather than announced. A useful test: if the studies could be reordered without the argument changing, there is no argument yet."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-1"}><span>{"What is the difference between a literature review and a gap analysis?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"A literature review says what is known. A gap analysis says what is not, and does it precisely enough to act on. They are usually sold together because the second is impossible without the first, but they are different pieces of work and the second is where most reviews stop short. A real gap analysis names four things: which population and which outcome have never been studied together, where the evidence exists but rests on designs too weak to support the claims made from it, where studies contradict each other, and which group has been excluded from all of it. Each one is then written as a question a study could answer, with the design that would answer it."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-2"}><span>{"Which type of review do I actually need?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Work backwards from what it has to survive. A thesis chapter usually needs a critical or integrative review, unless your examiner specified systematic — in which case nothing else will do, and finding that out late is expensive. A grant background needs a scoping review with a strong gap analysis, because the panel is assessing the gap rather than the synthesis. A clinical evaluation report under EU MDR needs a systematic, documented search because a notified body will audit the method. A journal submission needs whatever type the journal publishes, which for review articles is often narrower than authors expect. And if you want to publish the review itself rather than use it as background, systematic or scoping is usually the only route, because narrative reviews are increasingly hard to place."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-3"}><span>{"How do I select and organise studies efficiently?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Write the inclusion and exclusion criteria before you start reading, in enough detail that two people would apply them the same way — that single step saves more time than any tool. Then search with controlled vocabulary rather than keywords, because MeSH and Emtree find what a phrase search misses, and follow it with citation searching in both directions on the papers that matter most. Manage everything in EndNote, Mendeley or Zotero from the first search, not from the point at which it becomes unmanageable. And organise into a matrix rather than into folders: one row per study, one column per attribute you will later want to group by. Folders let you find a paper; a matrix lets you see a pattern."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-4"}><span>{"How do I critically analyse and synthesise rather than summarise?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Summarising describes each study in turn. Synthesis makes the studies talk to each other, and the mechanical difference is what your sentences are about. If a sentence's subject is an author, you are summarising; if its subject is a finding, a disagreement or a limitation shared across several studies, you are synthesising. Critical analysis goes one step further and asks what each study's design can actually support — whether the sample justifies the generalisation, whether the outcome measured is the outcome claimed, whether the comparator was fair, and who funded it. The useful habit is to write the appraisal into the matrix as you read, because reconstructing it later from memory is where most reviews turn back into summaries."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-5"}><span>{"What goes wrong most often in literature reviews?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Seven things, in roughly this order. No focus, so the review describes a field rather than building towards a question. A structure that follows reading order rather than argument. Summarising where appraisal was needed. Literature that stops three years short, usually because the search was run once and never re-run. A search that cannot be reproduced from what the methods say, which is fatal in anything systematic. Referencing that does not match the studies described. And a conclusion that does not connect to the research objectives — a review that ends without the reader knowing what it was for. Six of the seven are set before any writing begins."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-6"}><span>{"How many sources should a literature review include?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"There is no number, and any service that quotes you one is pricing rather than advising. What matters is whether the search was complete against its own stated criteria. A narrow, well-defined clinical question might have forty eligible studies and a review that cites sixty is padding; a broad scoping question might return three hundred and citing forty would be a selection problem rather than an editorial choice. Where a word limit forces a cut, the honest approach is to state the criteria that decided what was cited and supply the full matrix as supplementary material — so the reader can see that the selection was systematic rather than convenient."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-7"}><span>{"What if the gap analysis finds that my question has already been answered?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Then we tell you, in the first week, and that is the most valuable thing this service does even though it is the least welcome. It is also rarely the end of the project. A question answered in one population is often open in another; a question answered by three weak studies is open to a well-designed one; a question answered in 2016 is open again if the technology or the standard of care has moved. What usually happens is that the question narrows rather than disappears — and a narrow question with a demonstrated gap is a considerably stronger proposal than the broad one you started with."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-8"}><span>{"Can you work from a draft I have already written?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-8"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, and a good deal of our work arrives that way. The first deliverable is a written critique rather than a revision, because it has to say honestly what is repairable. Structure, synthesis, appraisal, referencing and language all are — a review organised study by study can be restructured around themes in days. What cannot be repaired by editing is a search that was never systematic, or literature that stops before the last three years; both have to be re-run, and a rewrite that papers over either will fail with the next reader for exactly the same reason it failed with the last. Expert editing then handles the rest: clarity, logical flow, transitions, redundancy, consistent terminology and academic tone."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-9"}><span>{"Who is the author, and how is AI use declared?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-9"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"You are. Authorship under ICMJE requires substantial contribution to conception or design, or to acquisition, analysis or interpretation; drafting or critically revising; approving the final version; and agreeing to be accountable for it. Pubrica supports all four but takes none of them in your place, and we do not accept authorship on client work. Where our contribution should appear in the acknowledgements we say so and draft the wording. On artificial intelligence: any AI-assisted searching, screening or drafting is declared in the methods, with what was used and for which step, because ICMJE and COPE both require it now and an undeclared tool found afterwards is treated as a research integrity issue rather than a matter of style."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-10"}><span>{"How recent do the sources have to be?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-10"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"There is no rule, and the five-year convention some supervisors quote is a heuristic rather than a standard. What matters is whether the literature has moved. In a field where the measurement technique changed in 2019, a 2016 paper may be describing something no longer comparable; in a stable field, the 1998 paper may still be the definitive one and leaving it out looks like you have not read the area. The defensible approach is to state the date range and justify it in a sentence, then include the older work that is foundational and say why it is. An examiner objects to an unexplained cut-off far more often than to an old citation."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-11"}><span>{"Can I include preprints, theses and conference abstracts?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-11"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, with the status labelled. Excluding them entirely introduces exactly the publication bias a review is supposed to expose, and in fast-moving fields the preprint is often where the finding first appeared. What is not acceptable is presenting a preprint as though it were peer reviewed. We record publication status as a field in the extraction matrix, mark it in the evidence table, and where a conclusion depends materially on non-peer-reviewed evidence we say so in the limitations. Conference abstracts carry a particular caution: the published paper, when it appears, not infrequently reports different numbers, and the abstract rarely contains enough method to appraise."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-12"}><span>{"How is a literature review in a grant proposal different from one in a thesis?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-12"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Length and purpose, which change almost everything. A thesis review establishes that you have command of the field and can take a position within it; it can afford to be comprehensive and is read by people who will test its edges. A grant review has perhaps three hundred words, is read by someone deciding whether to keep reading, and exists to make one gap unavoidable. The thesis version cannot be cut down to the grant version — the selection criterion is different, not just the word count. Written properly, the grant version cites the three papers that close off every alternative explanation and nothing else."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-13"}><span>{"How do I avoid plagiarism and self-plagiarism in a literature review?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-13"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"A review is more exposed to both than any other section, because so much of it is other people’s work restated. Two practical rules do most of the work. Extract into a structured matrix rather than into prose, so that what you write later comes from fields you filled in rather than from sentences you half-remember. And when you are reusing your own earlier text — from a thesis, a protocol, an earlier paper — cite it, because journals treat undisclosed reuse as a research integrity issue rather than a stylistic one. We screen for similarity before delivery and send the report with the draft, flagged by source, so you can see what is quoted and what is coincidental."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"lr-14"}><span>{"Can a literature review be published as a standalone paper?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"lr-14"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, and it is a legitimate route to a citable output, though the bar has moved. Narrative reviews are increasingly asked to say how the literature was found, which is why SANRA exists as a quality scale for them and why many journals now expect at least a described search. If you want the review to carry weight, the choice is to make it systematic in method even if narrative in voice: state the databases, the dates, the inclusion criteria and the number of records, and report under PRISMA where it applies. A review that says how it found what it found is cited more and disputed less."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of the review."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A literature review is usually the first thing a project needs and the last thing it revisits."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"WHERE THE GAP LEADS"}</b><em>{"the study that closes it"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/experimental-design/"}><b>{"Experimental design"}</b><span>{"Turning a stated gap into a study that can actually answer it, powered and pre-registered."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/grant-writing/"}><b>{"Grant writing"}</b><span>{"The proposal the gap analysis was written for, with the background section already built."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"IF THE REVIEW GOES FURTHER"}</b><em>{"from mapping to synthesis"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/systematic-review/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Systematic review"}</b><span>{"A registered protocol, dual screening and risk-of-bias assessment, when the method itself has to be auditable."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/meta-analysis/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Meta-analysis"}</b><span>{"Pooled estimates where the studies you found are alike enough to combine, with heterogeneity explained."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"IF THE REVIEW IS THE PAPER"}</b><em>{"getting it published"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/journal-selection/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Journal selection"}</b><span>{"Which journals still publish review articles in your field, and which of them yours actually fits."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/peer-review-pre-submission/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Pre-submission peer review"}</b><span>{"The objection to your search or your synthesis, heard before an editor's reviewer makes it."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading on structure and journals."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces from our library on how review articles are built, chosen for and written."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"https://pubrica.com/academy/physician-writing/how-to-structure-case-reports-review-articles-journals/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How to structure case reports and review articles for medical journals"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Medical journals expect a set structure, with clear objectives and a reporting guideline behind each section."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-should-physicians-choose-the-right-journal-for-submitting-a-case-report/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How should physicians choose the right journal for submitting a case report?"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Publishing takes more than clinical knowledge; it demands a strategic read of which journals still publish what, and how."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-physicians-can-write-clear-and-impactful-patient-education-materials/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How physicians can write clear and impactful patient education materials"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Patient education materials carry health literacy. Clear ones change adherence; unclear ones quietly cost it."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send the topic. We will tell you what is missing."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Whether your question has already been answered, how much literature there is, which type of review your purpose calls for, and whether there is a gap narrow enough to build on — answered in two business days, at no cost and with no obligation."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
